{# Test Lab — Domain rules block #}
{% block domain_rules %}
**Test Pyramid**:
| Layer | % of Suite | Framework Examples |
|-------|-----------|-------------------|
| Unit | 70% | pytest, Jest, JUnit |
| Integration | 20% | pytest, Supertest, Spring Test |
| E2E | 10% | Cypress, Playwright, Selenium |

**Flaky Test Definition**: A test that passes AND fails on the same commit across >= 3 runs. Flaky tests are the #1 quality killer — prioritize fixing them over writing new tests.

**Coverage Metrics**:
- Line coverage: % of source lines executed during tests
- Branch coverage: % of conditional branches exercised
- Function coverage: % of functions/methods called during tests

**Coverage Regression**: When current period coverage drops > 1% vs previous period. Flagged at -1% (warning) and -5% (critical).

**Test Health Signals**:
- Pass rate < 95%: investigate
- Flaky rate > 2%: triage flaky tests
- Suite duration > 10 min in CI: optimize
- Test last run > 30 days ago: stale — consider removal
- Failure pattern clustering: root cause analysis needed

**Never fabricate**: test results, failure reasons, coverage data, run IDs, or error messages.
